52?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/partybusiness","html_url":"https://github.com/partybusiness","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/partybusiness/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/partybusiness/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/partybusiness/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/partybusiness/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/partybusiness/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/partybusiness/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/partybusiness/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/partybusiness/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/partybusiness/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-03T20:51:52Z","updated_at":"2026-04-03T20:51:52Z","body":"I've also encountered this when using a viewport texture with transparency.\n\nYes, I can compensate in the shader that displays the viewport texture, but I think it would be nice to have it as an option on the SubViewport whether or not to pre-multiply. That would make it more similar to imported textures, where there is an option in the import settings to premult alpha or not. As long as it defaults to on, it will be backwards compatible.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4185152974/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4367510359","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99715#issuecomment-4367510359","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99715","id":4367510359,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBFLrVw","user":{"login":"artmouse155","id":72361968,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcyMzYxOTY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/72361968?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/artmouse155","html_url":"https://github.com/artmouse155","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artmouse155/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artmouse155/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artmouse155/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artmouse155/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artmouse155/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artmouse155/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artmouse155/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artmouse155/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/artmouse155/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-04T00:05:47Z","updated_at":"2026-05-04T00:05:47Z","body":"I am encountering in 4.6.2 stable what I believe to be the issue discussed here. Here is a mockup demonstrating what I am experiencing. Note how the semi-transparent Godot sprites in the \"transparent bg\" subviewport appear darker than the other two sets of semi-transparent sprites:\n\n<img width=\"1254\" height=\"732\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5fbd2350-458d-4cdf-83e1-8a7536226c5f\" />","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4367510359/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4948818674","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/99715#issuecomment-4948818674","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99715","id":4948818674,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJvj68g","user":{"login":"Zylann","id":1311555,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzMTE1NTU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1311555?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann","html_url":"https://github.com/Zylann","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Zylann/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-11T21:27:38Z","updated_at":"2026-07-11T21:27:38Z","body":"I'm encountering this while making a tool to bake assets for a prototype using transparent viewports, and is causing them to be darker. My output are PNG files so using a \"premultiplied alpha\" material mode is not suitable.\n\nI can use this in GDScript over the viewport's output:\n```gdscript\nstatic func _unpremultiply_alpha(im: Image) -> void:\n\tfor y in im.get_height():\n\t\tfor x in im.get_width():\n\t\t\tvar col := im.get_pixel(x, y)\n\t\t\tif col.a <= 0.0:\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\tvar k := 1.0 / col.a\n\t\t\tcol.r *= k\n\t\t\tcol.g *= k\n\t\t\tcol.b *= k\n\t\t\tim.set_pixel(x, y, col)\n```\nHowever this requires a trip to CPU to run slowly and deteriorates color quality.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4948818674/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_git